  "note": "Source: picked round5.md and recovered the recovered drawing source (lines 140-164). True source geometry for pointy-top hex with sx=0.98, sy=1.05, quiff, circular eyewear, jacket with piping, feet, and drafting divider. Dynamic curve equations in chart panel captured via static variants (idle, thinking, converged, diverged). Gestures nod and wave use explicit root-rotation fallbacks. Rim stroke uses a flat source gold role: contract 3.5 types stroke as a role, although the accounting prose mentions gradient stroke invocations. Gradient-stroke authoring needs an explicit freeze decision; the fixture does not silently extend that field. Founder palette pick applied from the round-2 showcase: slate body #66889a, copper rim #d87349, slate jacket #3f5563, ink #1b2430/#0e141d; these deliberately differ from the round-5 source colours in the comparison. Retains the picked quiff and untinted wire glasses; no lens fill. Authored figure scale is 0.64 with a centred origin to retain the complete chart glow and divider motion inside the frame. Mouth ellipses use normalised kit coordinates."
